Upstream source: https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/34f7a6cd150fd7a166958d989d5abab56e9e3d15/Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Measure/Prokhorov.lean
Local adaptations: namespace, old RMK linear-map/positivity API, old Lean syntax
and locally checked compatibility changes. This does not backport the general
(noncompact-space) Prokhorov theorem.
OrbitAverage.lean is newly written for this project, not copied upstream.
KSEntropyJoin.lean and KSEntropyMono.lean are also copied from the same Marcel
Morgenstern commit 040fec2e0ddf4fcba49af9f76c866d295308dd7f. In addition to the
local import root, Mono imports the sufficient KSEntropyBounds dependency
instead of the unused KSEntropyProps wrapper. Original Apache headers retained.
FixedRefinement.lean and MixtureEntropy.lean are newly written for this project.
OrbitMixture.lean is newly written for this project.

Further conditional-entropy modules adapted from the same Marcel Morgenstern
commit: CondPartition, CondPullback, CondChainRule, CondMono,
CondEntropyContinuous, CondExpEquivariant, CondJointPullback, CondKSEntropy,
CondBlockSubadditive, CondKSEntropySystem, Generator,
CondGivenPartitionBridge, CondChainRuleSup, FactorGeneratorSaturate,
JoinSigmaAlgebra. FiniteConditionalEntropy is the finite-partition portion
split from upstream CondChainRule, with its original copyright header.
Compatibility changes include the pinned finite-sum, integrability, and
conditional-expectation APIs. Conditional Jensen in CondMono is proved here
by applying ordinary integral Jensen to the actual conditional probability
kernel; the newer ConditionalExpectation.CondJensen import is not available
in the pinned mathlib. The conditional-expectation pull-out identities use
the existing ConditionalExpectation.Real module.
ConditionalEntropy.lean, KSEntropyFuture.lean and
ConditionalEntropyNontrivial.lean are newly written for this project.
FutureKernelSupport.lean and SmallPositivePartition.lean are also newly
written for this project, not copied upstream.

